<title>COTE D'IVOIRE: Abidjan July cotton fibre exports half June level.</title>
<headline>Abidjan July cotton fibre exports half June level.</headline>
<dateline>ABIDJAN 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cotton fibre exports from Abidjan, Ivory Coast's main port, amounted to 14,132 tonnes in July against 28,649 tonnes in June, official data showed.</p>
<p>Exports in July 1995 were 33,395 tonnes.</p>
<p>Abidjan handles most of the cotton produced in neighbouring Burkina Faso and Mali as well as home-grown fibre.</p>
<p>A breakdown of exports by origin follows - (in tonnes)</p>
<p>			July 96	  June 96	  July 95</p>
<p> Ivory Coast	 3,264	    9,653	    12,247</p>
<p> Burkina Faso	5,381	   10,366	    12,310</p>
<p> Mali		  5,094	    8,291	     8,608</p>
<p> Unspecified	   393		339		 230</p>
<p> Total		14,132	   28,649	    33,395</p>
<p>About a third of Mali's output is exported via Dakar in Senegal and some of Burkina Faso's cotton is shipped from Togo's Lome port.</p>
<p>Cumulative January-July cotton exports from Abidjan were 203,710 tonnes this year and 219,318 tonnes last year.</p>
<p>San Pedro, Ivory Coast's other commercial port, handled no cotton last year and just 2,014 tonnes in the whole of 1994. It had no cotton shipments in the first five months of 1996. --David Gault, Abidjan Newsroom +225 21 90 90</p>
</text>
